  "question": {
    "text": "Visible light of wavelength <math><mn>6000</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> falls normally on a single slit and produces a diffraction pattern. It is found that the second diffraction minimum is at <math><msup><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> from the central maximum. If the first minimum is produced at <math><msub><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi></mi></math> then <math><msub><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> is close to"
